# Not a parity scenario: spellings at a permission question this unit does
# not change, for the units that own them. From choice 1: Shift-Down,
# Ctrl-Down, Super-Down, Ctrl-N, then Shift-Up, Ctrl-Up, Ctrl-P, each with a
# snap; `ESC ESC [ D` last, because xfx reads it as Escape and Left, and the
# Escape cancels the turn. The turns, the workspace and the settings are
# approvals.cap's.
fx: gateway approvals-fx.json
xfx: gateway approvals-xfx.json
work approvals-ws
fx: seed approvals-fx-settings.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
wait 3
type edit the files
key Enter
wait 3
snap ask
key S-Down
wait 0.4
snap shift-down
key C-Down
wait 0.4
snap ctrl-down
key -H 1b 5b 31 3b 39 42
wait 0.4
snap super-down
key -H 0e
wait 0.4
snap ctrl-n
key S-Up
wait 0.4
snap shift-up
key C-Up
wait 0.4
snap ctrl-up
key -H 10
wait 0.4
snap ctrl-p
key -H 1b 1b 5b 44
wait 0.6
snap esc-esc-left
